# A cell born of a bare integer literal is an `i64`, and a later write of
# another width is a mismatch that, until panel 209, named the two types and
# not the declaration where the repair is: the note names the birth and the
# guess annotates the cell with the width the write holds (the width class,
# 15 cells in 4 files of `selfhost/` at the sitting).

function main()
    n @= 0
    b: u8 = 255
    n @ b  #~ type_mismatch
    print(n)
